and objects for better organization and reusability.

ADVANTAGES:
    Provides a clear structure of programs
    Makes code easier to maintain, reuse and debug
    Helps keep you code clean

Class & Object:
Class: Attributes associated with a value
Create Class:
            class MyClass:
            x = 5
Methods: functions 

Object:
Create Object:
              p1 = MyClass()
              print(p1.x)
To access the variable in class we use dot function(.)

__init__(self)-constructor:
__init__() is called automatically when an object is created.
it is used to initialize obect attributes.
self refers to the current object.
__init__() can take parameters.
Every object gets its own copy of instance variables initialized thru self.

Types of Data Members:
1. Instance Data Member: Defined with self.
                         Each object gets its own copy.
                         Changes in one object do not affect other objects.

2. Class Data Member: Declared inside the class but outside the methods.
                      Shared by all objects of the class.
                      Only one copy exists.

3. Private Data Member: Begin with double underscore(__).
                        Cannot be directly accessed outside the class.
                        Used for data hiding and encapsulation.

